WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.930
Every AI idea starts the same way.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.990
An agent, by Friday, please!

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:07.990
Hold on.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.630
One word just answered three questions.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.310
What form it takes.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.970
How much it does on its own.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.970
What kind of AI it needs.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.230
Right Shape answers all three.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.790
You just describe the job.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.750
Take a support inbox that refunds small orders.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.490
It wants to run on its own.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.550
But it reads strangers' email.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.150
And it moves money!

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.170
So it lands on rung five, right alongside you, until the refund limit is set in code.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.350
Then it writes a test you can actually fail.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:46.850
A trap to catch.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.810
A case to leave alone.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.390
Most of the time, the right shape is smaller than you think.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:00:59.290
Right Shape.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.570
The easy way to extend your AI, the right way.
